        "product_faq_widget": {
          "type": "product-faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "FAQs",
            "product_faq_metafield": "custom.collection_faqs",
            "product_faq_limit": 5,
            "product_question_1": "What makes an Oushak rug special?",
            "product_answer_1": "<p>Oushak rugs are among the most celebrated traditional rugs in the world, known for their soft color palettes, large-scale motifs, and refined elegance.</p><p>At Bisha Rugs, each Oushak is handwoven by skilled artisans, ensuring every piece carries its own individuality and craftsmanship.</p>",
            "product_question_2": "What materials are used in your rugs?",
            "product_answer_2": "<p>Our Oushak rugs are made using premium natural wool, selected for its durability, softness, and ability to hold color beautifully over time. Natural fibers allow the rug to age gracefully while maintaining its structure and comfort underfoot.</p>",
            "product_question_3": "Will my rug look exactly like the photos?",
            "product_answer_3": "<p>Our photos represent the rug as accurately as possible. However, because each rug is handmade and natural fibers interact uniquely with dyes and lighting, slight variations in tone, texture, and pattern may occur. These subtle differences are part of the charm and authenticity of handcrafted rugs.</p>",
            "product_question_4": "Why invest in a handmade Oushak rug?",
            "product_answer_4": "<p>Unlike mass-produced rugs, a handwoven Oushak is crafted slowly and intentionally. The result is a piece that brings warmth, artistry, and lasting value to your home.</p>",
            "product_question_5": "Are size variations normal for handmade rugs?",
            "product_answer_5": "<p>Yes. Because Oushak rugs are woven by hand, small variations in size (typically within 3–5%) may occur. This is a natural result of traditional weaving techniques and is considered a hallmark of authentic craftsmanship.</p>",
            "shipping_faq_metafield": "",
            "shipping_faq_limit": 5,
            "shipping_question_1": "Do you ship internationally?",
            "shipping_answer_1": "<p>Yes, we ship worldwide. International orders may be subject to customs duties, taxes, or import fees determined by your country's regulations. These charges are the responsibility of the customer unless otherwise stated.</p>",
            "shipping_question_2": "How long does it take to receive my rug?",
            "shipping_answer_2": "<p>For in-stock rugs, orders are typically processed within 2–5 business days before shipping. For custom or made-to-order rugs, weaving timelines vary (normally 4 to 6 weeks) depending on size and complexity.</p><p>Once shipped, delivery within the United States typically takes 5–7 business days.</p>",
            "shipping_question_3": "Can I return my rug?",
            "shipping_answer_3": "<p>Returns are accepted for standard (non-custom) rugs within 7 days of delivery, provided the rug is unused and returned in original condition. Custom or made-to-order rugs are not eligible for return.</p>",
            "shipping_question_4": "What if my rug arrives damaged?",
            "shipping_answer_4": "<p>In the rare event that a rug arrives damaged during transit, please contact us within 48 hours of delivery with photographs of the rug and packaging. We will work quickly to resolve the issue with a replacement or appropriate solution.</p>",
            "shipping_question_5": "How can I contact Bisha Rugs?",
            "shipping_answer_5": "<p>We are always happy to assist with questions about sizing, design, or custom orders.</p><p><strong>Email:</strong> Love@bisharugs.com</p><p><strong>Website:</strong> https://bisharugs.com</p>"
          }
        },
